seg-95eeaa0033b3 = One GeoJSON file per source per UTC day, in the <c1/> directory, named <c2/>, where <c3/> is <c4/> or <c5/>, <c6/> is the <c7/> key (<c8/>, <c9/>, <c10/>, or <c11/>) and the date is the UTC day of the reports: <c12/>, <c13/>. The dataset is in the name so two datasets of one kind cannot share a file, and <b>Kshana never overwrites a file</b>: if any target exists the command fails before writing anything. The CLI prints one line per file it writes. A reader can recover the three parts with <c14/>; the same information is inside the file (<c15/>, <c16/>, <c17/>). Synthetic sample files, one per source, are in <c18/>, with the command that regenerates them, for building and testing a viewer. A top-level <c19/> member holds the schema name, date, grid, method id and every parameter, the day-level figures, the data licence and attribution, and a notice. Each feature is a cell polygon with <c20/>, <c21/>, <c22/>, <c23/> and the aggregate counts.

