seg-83b660b0bfa6 = Each airborne ADS-B report carries two self-assessed navigation quality fields: NIC (the containment radius of the position) and NACp (the { "95" }% accuracy bound, EPU). When the receiver on board loses or distrusts its satellite fix, both drop, which is why they carry a signature of interference. They also drop for other reasons.

