seg-206c78a69ded = Route exposure

# text
# c1: --route
# c2: lat,lon
# c3: --map
seg-0d8832796ab7 = <c1/> is a GeoJSON LineString (bare, in a Feature, or in a FeatureCollection) or a CSV of <c2/> lines. <c3/> takes map files or directories of them, and may be repeated. Waypoints are joined by straight lines in latitude and longitude, so densify long legs; a leg takes the short way round in longitude, so one that crosses the antimeridian ({ "179.5" } E to { "179.5" } W) crosses it. The route is split into pieces of about { "250" } m. Each piece is measured between its own two end points on a sphere of radius { "6371.0088" } km (the same path that decides which cell it lies in) and assigned to the cell holding its midpoint.

# text
# c1: share_degraded
# c2: share_not_degraded
# c3: share_unassessed
# c4: share_not_observed
seg-cc5e2553700b = Per day and per source the report gives the route length and four shares that sum to { "1" }: <c1/>, <c2/>, <c3/> (cell present but without a call) and <c4/> (cell absent from the map). Read the last two with the first: a route with a low degraded share and a high not-observed share has not been shown to be clear. ADS-B and AIS rows are reported separately and never combined. Each row carries the map's licence and attribution.

