seg-0de37085f544 = <c1/> compares Kshana with independent implementations on synthetic inputs, with tolerances pre-registered in <c2/>: NIC and NACp code meanings against pyModeS decoding of synthetic ADS-B frames, AIS not-available values against pyais decoding of synthetic AIVDM sentences, grid cell assignment against shapely, route length per cell state against shapely and GeographicLib, and inland masking against shapely and pyproj. The fixtures are made by <c3/>; CI needs no Python. This validates how the codes and field values are read and the geometry. It does not validate that a flagged cell is interference.

